{"Title":"An Act relative to the consideration of ergonomically designed school buildings","BillNumber":"H553","DocketNumber":"HD887","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T12:42:16.177"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T12:42:16.1766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H553/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Philips of Sharon, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 553) of Edward R. Philips relative to the feasibility of ergonomically designed school buildings and its beneficial impact on students and faculty.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding the provisions of any general or special law to the contrary, Chapter 70B, section 2 of the general laws, as appearing in the 2006 official edition, is hereby amended by including herein the following definition: \r\n\tErgonomics:  the scientific discipline concerned with designing to physical, cognitive, and organizational needs of students and educators, in an effort to optimize safety, comfort and ease of use, productivity, and performance. \r\n\tSECTION 2. Chapter 70B, section 3 shall be amended by adding section 3(x):\r\n\tto consider the feasibility of the integration of ergonomic models appropriate for classrooms and laboratories within the scope of the construction or rehabilitation of a particular proposal; the investment of brick and mortar, and its beneficial impact to the students and faculty of the school.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}